 B is correct. The value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_004_2a797a9f.png\" alt=\"f of 9 minus f of 1 \"></span> can be calculated by finding the values of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_005_11a2ecc7.png\" alt=\"f of 9 \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_006_bd1521c1.png\" alt=\"f of 1\"></span>. The value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_007_11a2ecc7.png\" alt=\"f of 9 \"></span> can be found by substituting 9 for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in the given function: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_008_d01dd173.png\" alt=\"f of 9 equals, the fraction with numerator, open parenthesis, 9 plus 7, close parenthesis, and denominator 4\"></span>. This equation can be rewritten as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_009_02b68bb0.png\" alt=\"f  of 9 equals, 16 over 4\"></span>, or 4. Then, the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_010_bd1521c1.png\" alt=\"f of 1\"></span> can be found by substituting 1 for <span class=\"italic\">x </span>in the given function: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_011_83d50e32.png\" alt=\"f of 1 equals, the fraction with numerator, open parenthesis, 1 plus 7, close parenthesis, and denominator 4\"></span></span>. This equation can be rewritten as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_012_8e36c512.png\" alt=\"f of 1 equals, 8 over 4\"></span>, or 2. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/271f7e3f/img_013_fbae3b2b.png\" alt=\"f of 9 minus f of 1, equals, 4 minus 2\"></span>, which is equivalent to 2.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from incorrectly substituting values of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in the given function or making computational errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":14,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959618,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"271f7e3f","skill_cd":"H.B.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Linear functions","createDate":1691007959618,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"022313-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"6c56b405-05fc-4cc6-8148-e5fec64cd1cb","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"022313-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of x equals, the fraction with numerator x plus 7, and denominator 4\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">For the function <span class=\"italic\">f</span> defined above, what is the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 9, minus, f of 1\"></span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>1</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p>2</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"one fourth\"></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"nine fourths\"></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 9 minus f of 1 \"></span> can be calculated by finding the values of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 9 \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 1\"></span>. The value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 9 \"></span> can be found by substituting 9 for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in the given function: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 9 equals, the fraction with numerator, open parenthesis, 9 plus 7, close parenthesis, and denominator 4\"></span>. This equation can be rewritten as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f  of 9 equals, 16 over 4\"></span>, or 4. Then, the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 1\"></span> can be found by substituting 1 for <span class=\"italic\">x </span>in the given function: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 1 equals, the fraction with numerator, open parenthesis, 1 plus 7, close parenthesis, and denominator 4\"></span></span>. This equation can be rewritten as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 1 equals, 8 over 4\"></span>, or 2. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"f of 9 minus f of 1, equals, 4 minus 2\"></span>, which is equivalent to 2.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from incorrectly substituting values of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in the given function or making computational errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959618,"updateDate":1691007959618}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959618, 1691007959618),
