 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>24</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"8 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>8</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>24</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"96 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>96</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>24</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554987,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"2e8cc1c0","skill_cd":"H.A.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Linear equations in one variable","createDate":1743430554987,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"","external_id":"cb01072a-91f8-4bc2-b74f-51d996629f69","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"99265cf5-cdd5-4d58-9cc2-e28da798ddab","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If <math alttext=\"4 x equals 3\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, what is the value of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["1b9b75d7-2577-4108-b809-c41adab72bda"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"fe05e018-72bf-4f2a-baff-e7c489241d24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"nine halves\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7e304356-0684-4c41-8eed-2d1fc7a4836b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1b9b75d7-2577-4108-b809-c41adab72bda","content":"<p><math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"bab7f7bb-8af5-4194-87bb-f77a012e0edb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"4 x equals 3\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"24 x equals 18\"><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>24</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"6 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>6</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>24</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"8 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>8</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>24</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"96 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>96</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"24 x\"><mrow>\n<mn>24</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>","externalid":"cb01072a-91f8-4bc2-b74f-51d996629f69","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1743430554987,"updateDate":1743430554987}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554987, 1743430554987),
    ($SATQ$2e98b1df$SATQ$, $SATQ$96677815-bb45-424b-a4e5-ec40dbe43bb8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in one variable$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">On the first day of a semester, a film club has <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math> members. Each day after the first day of the semester, <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> new members join the film club. If no members leave the film club, how many total members will the film club have <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> days after the first day of the semester?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"96043a84-d961-4ae6-93d6-fcb3373c2cdc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"400\"><mn>400</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"006e69ba-7a3c-4f1f-8e91-bf2836fde2d2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"130\"><mn>130</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c708641f-5c32-4590-8f9c-b21bed0231f5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"94\"><mn>94</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5e6a7a6c-65d5-4eb1-9fa2-38987b3c51fb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["006e69ba-7a3c-4f1f-8e91-bf2836fde2d2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the film club has <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math> members on the first day of a semester, and <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> new members join the film club each day after the first day of the semester. This means that after <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> days, <math alttext="4 times 10"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, or <math alttext="40"><mn>40</mn>
</math>, new members will have joined the club. Adding <math alttext="40"><mn>40</mn>
</math> members to the original <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math> club members yields <math alttext="130"><mn>130</mn>
</math> members. Thus, the film club will have <math alttext="130"><mn>130</mn>
</math> total members <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> days after the first day of the semester.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of members that will have joined the film club <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> days after the first day of the semester if <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math> new members, not <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>, join the film club each day.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the number of members the film club will have <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> days after the first day of the semester if <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> new member, not <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>, joins the film club each day.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the number of members the film club has on the first day of the semester.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"2e98b1df","external_id":"96677815-bb45-424b-a4e5-ec40dbe43bb8","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"9011420c-7409-4212-904d-87b41928755f","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.A.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in one variable","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">On the first day of a semester, a film club has <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math> members. Each day after the first day of the semester, <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> new members join the film club. If no members leave the film club, how many total members will the film club have <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> days after the first day of the semester?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"96043a84-d961-4ae6-93d6-fcb3373c2cdc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"400\"><mn>400</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"006e69ba-7a3c-4f1f-8e91-bf2836fde2d2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"130\"><mn>130</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c708641f-5c32-4590-8f9c-b21bed0231f5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"94\"><mn>94</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5e6a7a6c-65d5-4eb1-9fa2-38987b3c51fb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["006e69ba-7a3c-4f1f-8e91-bf2836fde2d2"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the film club has <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math> members on the first day of a semester, and <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> new members join the film club each day after the first day of the semester. This means that after <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> days, <math alttext=\"4 times 10\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</m