<p style="text-align: left;">What is the solution&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to the given system of equations?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"c5d09b22-8d61-437c-b63a-f529bbf2157c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 15 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"45e61160-dcb5-46f6-862f-a8a9d1ef7267","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 16 comma 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"87133788-189d-42dd-a00f-ff20910793dd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 17 comma 1 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"9ee7bda9-b11f-4009-b785-e0254069ca76","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 18 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c5d09b22-8d61-437c-b63a-f529bbf2157c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. The second equation in the given system defines the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> as <math alttext="5 y"><mrow>
	<mn>5</mn>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="5 y"><mrow>
	<mn>5</mn>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> into the first equation yields <math alttext="5 y plus y equals 18"><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math> or <math alttext="6 y equals 18"><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="y equals 3"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>3</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the second equation yields&nbsp;<math alttext="5 left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis equals x"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> or <math alttext="x equals 15"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>. Therefore, the solution&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to the given system of equations is <math alttext="left parenthesis 15 comma 3 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. Substituting <math alttext="16"><mn>16</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the second equation yields&nbsp;<math alttext="5 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis equals 16"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>, which is not true. Therefore,&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 16 comma 2 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is not a solution to the given system of equations.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. Substituting <math alttext="17"><mn>17</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the second equation yields&nbsp;<math alttext="5 left parenthesis 1 right parenthesis equals 17"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math>, which is not true. Therefore,&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 17 comma 1 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is not a solution to the given system of equations.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. Substituting <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the second equation yields&nbsp;<math alttext="5 left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis equals 18"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>, which is not true. Therefore,&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 18 comma 0 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is not a solution to the given system of equations.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"317e80f9","external_id":"f0975e35-afbb-4d74-9091-7a06a2bf4d03","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"63fbfbeb-d7f4-484d-a54e-b1484140ac15","uId":"3c99ae45-761f-4502-8b01-a175f4094aea","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.D.","skill_desc":"Systems of two linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"x plus y equals 18\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>18</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"5 y equals x\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the solution&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to the given system of equations?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"c5d09b22-8d61-437c-b63a-f529bbf2157c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 15 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"45e61160-dcb5-46f6-862f-a8a9d1ef7267","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 16 comma 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></